# The C# toolchain lock, one file (cleat#4080, C# PR 2): everything `cleat build --target csharp` and the SDK's unit tests are allowed
# to run. Sourced by build.sh; the Go side reads the same file to name the cache volumes, so a change here starts a fresh cache
# rather than mixing packages from two locks. The digest, not the tag, is the pin. Nothing here was tested at any other version
# (cleat#4077, WS-cleat2's PINS.md). The package list and its hashes are in toolchain.packages.tsv.

# The one SDK image every C# step runs in: unit tests, fixture build, `cleat build`. The compiler only runs on Linux x64 or Windows,
# so the image is always the linux/amd64 one, emulated on an arm64 host.
# The digest is a MULTI-ARCH manifest list (measured 2026-11-18: linux/amd64 ddbaedfc..., linux/arm64 35c2411e..., linux/arm/v7), so
# one pin serves both platforms below; docker picks the manifest by --platform.
CLEAT_CS_SDK_IMAGE=mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:10.0@sha256:fe0fd4e93bd2fbb47c883b7a6369e5c8d3db8bf01cdc5981f6ee35fbdf3ff4fb

# Platforms the build is measured on. build.sh picks the one that matches the host (arm64 on Apple Silicon and arm64 Linux, amd64
# elsewhere); CLEAT_CS_PLATFORM in the environment overrides it. An arm64 host that builds linux/amd64 runs it under emulation (about
# 15 times slower, measured). Both produced a BYTE-IDENTICAL component for the test project (cleat#4080, measured 2026-11-18).
CLEAT_CS_PLATFORMS="linux/amd64 linux/arm64"

# wasi-sdk 29 is downloaded from GitHub and checked against this sha256 ONCE, into the cache volume, and used from there; the
# componentize package would otherwise download its own 119 MB copy on every build, unverified. Both hashes were computed from the downloads
# (upstream publishes none), so each is the hash of one download by one person, not a published checksum:
#   amd64: WS-cleat2, for cleat#4077; recorded in engine/testdata/csharp_defer_order/PINS.md, which gives no date (it landed with
#          #4082 on 2026-11-18); 119,441,678 bytes.
#   arm64: WS-cleat1, 2026-11-18, `shasum -a 256` of the file fetched from the URL below; 119,258,587 bytes.
# build.sh re-checks the hash on every cold install, in the container, so a later upstream replacement of either file is UNMEASURED.
#
# It is installed at ~/.wasi-sdk/wasi-sdk-29.0 EXACTLY, because the componentize package sets WASI_SDK_PATH to that path itself
# (BytecodeAlliance.Componentize.DotNet.WitBindgen.targets, overriding the environment) and downloads its own HARDCODED x86_64
# tarball, unverified, when the directory is absent. An earlier version of build.sh verified a different directory, so its check
# guarded something the build never used; build.sh now fails (UNMEASURED) if that download ever runs.
CLEAT_CS_WASISDK_VERSION=29.0
CLEAT_CS_WASISDK_URL_AMD64=https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk/releases/download/wasi-sdk-29/wasi-sdk-29.0-x86_64-linux.tar.gz
CLEAT_CS_WASISDK_SHA256_AMD64=87d1d1a2879d139cdc624b968efad3d4a97b8078cdff95e63ac88ecafd1a0171
CLEAT_CS_WASISDK_URL_ARM64=https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk/releases/download/wasi-sdk-29/wasi-sdk-29.0-arm64-linux.tar.gz
CLEAT_CS_WASISDK_SHA256_ARM64=052ad773397dc9e5aa99fb4cfef694175e6b1e81bb2ad1d3c8e7b3fc81441b7c
